LMS – Progress Calculation Implementation Summary
Here is what we have implemented so far.
1. Database and Models
- Added pages JSON column to the lessons table.
- Stored lesson documentation as pages containing title and content.
- LessonProgress tracks:
  - Total pages
  - Completed pages
  - Progress percentage
  - Status
- UserCourse tracks overall course progress.
2. Trailblazer Operations
LessonProgress::Operation::NextPage
- Finds the learner's course assignment.
- Finds the lesson progress.
- Checks whether previous lessons are completed.
- Fetches the next available page.
- Prevents fetching pages after completion.
LessonProgress::Operation::CompletePage
- Finds the learner's assignment and lesson progress.
- Checks previous lesson completion.
- Validates page number.
- Prevents skipping pages or completing the same page twice.
- Updates completed page count.
- Calls the progress calculation service.
3. Progress Services
Created three service classes inside app/services/progress/:
Service	Responsibility
LessonCalculator	Calculates individual lesson progress and status.
CourseCalculator	Calculates overall course progress and status.
Updater	Coordinates both calculations and saves updated records.

4. Progress Calculation Logic
- Lesson progress is calculated using completed pages and passed lesson quizzes.
- Course progress is calculated using completed pages and passed quizzes.
- Course status is maintained as:
  - assigned
  - in_progress
  - completed
- Lesson status is maintained as:
  - not_started
  - in_progress
  - completed
- Completed lesson count is updated automatically.
5. Controller – LessonProgressesController
Implemented two API actions:
- next_page – returns the next documentation page.
- complete_page – completes a page and returns updated lesson and course progress.
Both actions call Trailblazer operations and return JSON responses.
6. Routes
Configured:
GET  /user_courses/:user_course_id/lessons/:lesson_id/next_page

POST /user_courses/:user_course_id/lessons/:lesson_id/complete_page


